AU  - Elgaroy, O
AU  - Hannestad, S
TI  - Can Planck-scale physics be seen in the cosmic microwave background? - art. no. 123513
T2  - PHYSICAL REVIEW D
AB  - We investigate the potential of observations of anisotropies in the cosmic microwave background (CMB) and large-scale structure in the Universe to detect possible modifications of standard inflationary models by physics beyond the Planck scale. A generic model of the primordial density fluctuations is investigated, and we derive constraints on its parameters from current data. We conclude that the currently available data do not put very stringent constraints on this model. Furthermore, we use simulated power spectra from the Sloan Digital Sky Survey (SDSS) and the Planck satellite to show that it is unlikely that a trans-Planckian signature of this type can be detected in CMB and large-scale structure data.
